<%#
  One 24px round avatar for a leaderboard row - shared by Top Chatters and Most Mentioned on
  /<channel>/statistics/chat so the two boards, which sit side by side, keep identical row
  geometry. A missing avatar (profile-cache miss, Helix down, or a mentioned login that resolves
  to no account at all) falls back to a monogram rather than an empty box: same 24px, so the rows
  stay line-for-line aligned either way.

  alt is empty on purpose - the row's next element is the same person's name as real text, so a
  screen reader would otherwise read it twice.

  Params: url (string | null), name (string - the monogram's source).
%>
<% if (url) { %>
  <img src="<%= url %>" alt="" width="24" height="24" loading="lazy"
       class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full ring-1 ring-neutral-800 shrink-0" />
<% } else { %>
  <span aria-hidden="true"
        class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full grid place-items-center bg-neutral-800 text-neutral-400 text-[10px] font-semibold ring-1 ring-neutral-800 shrink-0"><%= (name || "?").charAt(0).toUpperCase() %></span>
<% } %>
